<details class="permission-explainer"><summary><MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.Info" Size="Size.Small" aria-hidden="true"/> Token validation explained</summary><div class="permission-comparison"><section><strong>Authenticate the token</strong><div class="permission-route">Access token → ASP.NET Core → API</div><p>JWT bearer middleware validates the signature, trusted issuer, expiry and audience. For v2 access tokens, the audience is the API’s client ID. Reject missing or invalid tokens with 401.</p></section><section><strong>Authorize the operation</strong><div class="permission-route">Valid token + required permission → Allow</div><p>Delegated calls need the required scope in scp; application calls need the required app role in roles. A valid token without the required permission returns 403.</p></section></div><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/scenario-protected-web-api-app-configuration" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Learn: protect a web API ↗</a></details>
